to run a freaking marathon to just get here.

00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:16.400
However, before he even has the opportunity&nbsp;
to exact revenge on this Rat, Kenzan is simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:16.400 --> 00:55:21.520
headshot and killed as collateral damage in&nbsp;
battle between Saitama and Tatsumaki. Screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:21.520 --> 00:55:26.840
that he’s a stubborn loser, Tatsumaki proceeds&nbsp;
to throw Saitama through another 3 buildings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:26.840 --> 00:55:32.360
Coming to a stop, Saitama tells the esper to&nbsp;
relax, like the whole reason for coming out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:32.360 --> 00:55:38.920
here to start with was to prevent damage.&nbsp;
Metal Bat having watched this and just not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:38.920 --> 00:55:43.720
in the mood after sprinting all the way to&nbsp;
the scene, decides to calm down and go home.

00:55:45.400 --> 00:55:50.240
Remember how Sweet Mask was over at that&nbsp;
meeting shunning the bubbly boys or whatever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:50.240 --> 00:55:53.360
well turns out the three buildings&nbsp;
Tatsumaki three Saitama threw was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:54.080 --> 00:55:56.400
directly opposite the building Mask was in.

00:55:56.400 --> 00:56:01.160
Noticing they have gone far from their original&nbsp;
location, Saitama suggests to Tatsumaki that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:01.160 --> 00:56:06.480
both of them head back. Tatsumaki at first seems&nbsp;
cooperative, dropping down and agreeing with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:06.480 --> 00:56:10.960
but after he points out the direction they should&nbsp;
travel. She proceeds to grab Saitama by his clean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:10.960 --> 00:56:15.040
shiny bald head and leads him back to their&nbsp;
original location by running his head into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:15.040 --> 00:56:19.720
the ground at the same time. Looking back&nbsp;
while being dragged, Saitama points out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:19.720 --> 00:56:23.760
there’s someone behind them. Breaking into&nbsp;
an inner monologue, Tatsumaki knows that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:24.440 --> 00:56:27.960
he’s able to keep up with them, then he must be a&nbsp;
monster or a hero. Genius deductive skills their.

00:56:27.960 --> 00:56:32.120
Turns out the feign behind them is the&nbsp;
ball banging legend Speed-o-Sound Sonic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:32.120 --> 00:56:35.880
who for some reason had a feeling that the&nbsp;
man being treated like a ragdoll was none&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:35.880 --> 00:56:40.480
other than Saitama. Unconcerned for the&nbsp;
previous scuffle, Speed throws a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:45.440
his weapons forth in an attempt to finally end&nbsp;
his rivals life. These special ninja shurikens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:45.440 --> 00:56:50.560
have been specifically engineered into a homing&nbsp;
version that will track its target then explode.

00:56:50.560 --> 00:56:55.480
Noticing them, Tatsumaki nonchalantly redirects&nbsp;
the shurikens back at the ninja catching him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:55.480 --> 00:57:00.560
completely by surprise. In an instant he begins&nbsp;
dodging each of his own attacks, yet he fails to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:00.560 --> 00:57:05.440
notice a nearby dog pooping on the floor and&nbsp;
accidentally steps in it. Losing his balance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:12.720
Speed curses Saitama while simultaneously&nbsp;
getting hit by his own exploding shurikens.

00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:16.280
After seeing that there now back at their&nbsp;
initial location, Saitama breaks loose from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:16.280 --> 00:57:20.000
Tatsumaki's grip, astonishing her with his&nbsp;
speed before telling her that she can feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:20.000 --> 00:57:26.440
free to rampage here! Annoyed at him looking&nbsp;
down on her, Tatsumaki clarifies that she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:26.440 --> 00:57:29.640
actually the one testing Saitama and claims&nbsp;
that due to his insolence she should go all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:29.640 --> 00:57:33.640
out and put him in his place. LITERALLY&nbsp;
CHILLING with his hand in his pocket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:38.400
Saitama tells her to go all-out on&nbsp;
him, which once again surprises her.

00:57:38.400 --> 00:57:42.960
Back inside the Hero Association headquarters,&nbsp;
many frustrated members of the Blizzard Group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:42.960 --> 00:57:48.280
quit being Hero’s after Fubuki's decision to break&nbsp;
up her group. This is just mainly because to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:48.280 --> 00:57:53.400
this group made them feel apart of something&nbsp;
bigger and stronger. Now with no leader they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:53.400 --> 00:57:58.440
lack any direction and aren't strong enough&nbsp;
themselves to compete with stronger Hero’s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:58.440 --> 00:58:03.000
However, Eyelashes isn't done and even manages&nbsp;
to motivate the few remaining loyal members to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:03.000 --> 00:58:07.280
follow him as he starts climbing towards&nbsp;
the surface in an attempt to find Fubuki.

00:58:07.280 --> 00:58:11.320
Up on the surface, Fubuki witnesses&nbsp;
tornadoes, along with a multitude of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:11.320 --> 00:58:15.720
differing sized boulders, smashing into and&nbsp;
devastating the landscape due to Tatsumaki's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:15.720 --> 00:58:20.840
increased psychic output. She screams out&nbsp;
to her sister that this is to much and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:20.840 --> 00:58:25.840
needs to stop, but is quickly forgotten about&nbsp;
as Tatsumaki beams Saitama through the sky.

00:58:25.840 --> 00:58:29.560
Over in the new base, King is seen at&nbsp;
the entrance of Saitama's apartment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:29.560 --> 00:58:33.080
is panicking due to the surrounding&nbsp;
catastrophe. Wondering where Saitama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:33.080 --> 00:58:36.720
could possibly be at a time like this,&nbsp;
our bald prophet suddenly shows up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:36.720 --> 00:58:40.360
crashing into the wall and telling King that&nbsp;
he’s currently too busy to play fighting games&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:40.360 --> 00:58:45.400
with him cause he’s dealing with something.&nbsp;
Curious as to who he’s fighting, King inquires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:45.400 --> 00:58:51.040
only to find out its this lil pipsqueak called&nbsp;
Tatsumaki. Having heard Saitama make fun of her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:51.040 --> 00:58:56.400
Tatsumaki dives in for a kick but misses&nbsp;
and instead crashes into the wall. Of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:56.400 --> 00:59:04.480
King catches a glimpse of Tatsumaki's underwear,&nbsp;
stunning him. Not giving it away, King just stands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:04.480 --> 00:59:10.120
there looking composed and ready for anything&nbsp;
as Tatsumaki glides back towards the bald man.

00:59:10.120 --> 00:59:13.920
As the intense showdown continues to&nbsp;
evolve, it sends even more tremors in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:13.920 --> 00:59:19.880
the direction of the Hero Association.&nbsp;
Forte and Air to wonder what is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:19.880 --> 00:59:23.040
on, even cockily mentioning that they might&nbsp;
head out to save the day. Scaring the life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:23.040 --> 00:59:28.920
out of Forte, Saitama crashes into the wall just&nbsp;
above his room. Confused he inquires as to why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:28.920 --> 00:59:33.680
he’s out here, prompting Saitama to ask him about&nbsp;
how his injuries are healing. Continuing to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:33.680 --> 00:59:37.320
the young hero to stay in bed, the caped&nbsp;
baldy leaps from the side of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:37.320 --> 00:59:40.760
back towards the midst of destruction.&nbsp;
After seeing the destruction that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:40.760 --> 00:59:45.840
fellow A-Class hero left to join, Forte decides&nbsp;
to wait a while before his rematch with him.

00:59:45.840 --> 00:59:49.200
Arriving at the surface themselves, the&nbsp;
remnants of the blizzard group is left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:49.200 --> 00:59:53.480
gobsmacked after seeing just how out of&nbsp;
control Tatsumaki is. They know that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:53.480 --> 00:59:57.400
they want to stick with Fubuki though,&nbsp;
they need to be marked by this beast.

00:59:57.400 --> 01:00:02.880
Swooping in over the C-Class Hero’s, Tatsumaki&nbsp;
knows she ended up miscalculating the outputted&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:02.880 --> 01:00:06.920
power of her limits limit. To start with&nbsp;
she was meant to be testing this guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:11.680
yet its all flipped on its head now. Up until&nbsp;
now, there has truly never been an opponent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:11.680 --> 01:00:18.280
that was able to take her head on. In all&nbsp;
actuality she was enjoying this battle as&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:18.280 --> 01:00:23.160
before it she’d assumed that the only person&nbsp;
capable of standing against her was blast.

01:00:24.280 --> 01:00:28.720
Needing to bring this pointless show of strength&nbsp;
to an end, Tatsumaki begins tearing up the ground&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:28.720 --> 01:00:32.840
and contorting all of the rubble into two&nbsp;
large waves that clash into each other. Apon&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:32.840 --> 01:00:37.880
forming a tunnel like structure, the esper then&nbsp;
collapse it apon the ant sized man underneath.

01:00:37.880 --> 01:00:42.640
Not even a fraction of a second later, Saitama&nbsp;
performs an effortlessly unharmed swing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:42.640 --> 01:00:46.320
throwing his arm up and dispersing all&nbsp;
of the rubble around him. Dropping to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:46.320 --> 01:00:50.200
the ground exhausted due to the&nbsp;
psychic output, Saitama jokes&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:50.200 --> 01:00:54.400
that she doesn't need to push herself and&nbsp;
should still have enough strength to talk.

01:00:55.760 --> 01:00:59.840
Snapping at him, the esper catches&nbsp;
Saitama in an orb of her psychic energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:59.840 --> 01:01:04.160
however he’s so damn heavy that she’s barely&nbsp;
able to even pick him up of the floor. Asking&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:04.160 --> 01:01:09.480
why she’s looking so grumpy? Saitama re-iterates&nbsp;
that he isn't her enemy. Like he mentioned before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:09.480 --> 01:01:13.960
its just she views the lives of human&nbsp;
relationships too lightly. For example&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:13.960 --> 01:01:17.720
right now she's being stopped by the&nbsp;
power of Fubuki’s mere acquaintance.

01:01:17.720 --> 01:01:21.200
Hearing those words and after&nbsp;
failing to send Saitama into space,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:21.200 --> 01:01:26.080
Tatsumaki slowly loses consciousness from&nbsp;
overusing her power. Dropping to her knee’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:26.080 --> 01:01:31.480
she starts to remember how Blast told her that she&nbsp;
shouldn't ever expect someone to come save her.

01:01:31.480 --> 01:01:37.760
Moments after Blast had saved her, Tatsumaki&nbsp;
reunited with Fubuki in order to protect her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:37.760 --> 01:01:42.160
After noticing she was followed by four&nbsp;
Tsukuyomi members, Tatsumaki disposed of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:42.160 --> 01:01:47.040
them before once again asking Fubuki to come with&nbsp;
her. The shock of witnessing her sister's violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:47.040 --> 01:01:52.160
acts caused the 5-year-old Fubuki to awaken&nbsp;
her psychic power and push Tatsumaki away.

01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:54.200
As this self-reflection of her’s continues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:54.200 --> 01:01:58.920
she comes to see it was her that dragged&nbsp;
Fubuki to a harsh fate. Because of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:58.920 --> 01:02:04.440
she now feels like she has the responsibility&nbsp;
to protect her without relying on anyone else.

01:02:04.440 --> 01:02:09.000
Actually crazy to realize the reason behind&nbsp;
Tatsumaki wanting to constantly protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:09.000 --> 01:02:15.720
her sister, was because she is the reason she&nbsp;
developed powers and now feels responsible for it.

01:02:17.480 --> 01:02:23.440
Awaking in a bright place, Tatsumaki see’s Blast&nbsp;
standing in the distance. Walking upto him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:23.440 --> 01:02:27.360
she asks if this is where he’s&nbsp;
been all along. Seeing him leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:27.360 --> 01:02:31.040
she cant help but run after him&nbsp;
and plead for him to not leave.

01:02:31.040 --> 01:02:36.560
Throughout the story so far, the only one to&nbsp;
set Tatsumaki free was Blast. Due to this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:41.400
she grew an obsessive excessive expectation&nbsp;
of Blast. She sought respect from the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:41.400 --> 01:02:45.080
that free’d her and needed someone&nbsp;
to guide her on a better road.

01:02:45.080 --> 01:02:48.680
Catching upto him know, Tatsumaki&nbsp;
just says that she tried really hard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:48.680 --> 01:02:53.120
but nothing ever works out. She doesn't&nbsp;
want everyone to hate and be afraid of her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:53.120 --> 01:02:56.760
but if they aren't then things will&nbsp;
just end up how they were before.

01:02:56.760 --> 01:02:58.720
Standing there with tears in here eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:58.720 --> 01:03:03.760
she questions the top-ranking hero about&nbsp;
what she should do? When suddenly a beam&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:03.760 --> 01:03:07.480
of light begins cutting its way&nbsp;
into this already glistening realm.

01:03:07.480 --> 01:03:11.800
Of course she was just waking up and&nbsp;
above her was the gleaming bald king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:11.800 --> 01:03:14.840
Saitama looking down and&nbsp;
asking if she was alright.

01:03:15.920 --> 01:03:20.840
Saitama praises Tatsumaki's abilities, and pats&nbsp;
her on the head while stating that if Tatsumaki&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:20.840 --> 01:03:26.160
can rampage without destroying other people's&nbsp;
stuff, she would make a great hero. As Saitama&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:26.160 --> 01:03:32.080
turns to leave, Fubuki arrives and tells Tatsumaki&nbsp;
she has separated from her group. Joking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:32.080 --> 01:03:35.800
she likes the new attitude but it doesn't&nbsp;
seem as if her own group understands yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:35.800 --> 01:03:40.000
Fubuki turns around to see all of her&nbsp;
loyal members running up behind her.

01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:43.040
Seeing Tatsumaki glaring at the&nbsp;
lot of them, Eyelashes along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:43.040 --> 01:03:46.120
a few of the other members garner up the&nbsp;
courage to asks her if she’ll allow them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:46.120 --> 01:03:51.840
to work below Fubuki. Done with these mice,&nbsp;
Tatsumaki raises her hand to annihilate them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:51.840 --> 01:03:55.720
however its Fubuki who jumps infront and&nbsp;
attacks her own men with a hell storm&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:55.720 --> 01:04:00.120
blast. Knowing that they came back here&nbsp;
to confront Tatsumaki, Fubuki questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:00.120 --> 01:04:05.000
what they hell they can even do? when they cant&nbsp;
fend off her drastically weaker psychic powers.

01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:10.120
Actually confused with what the fuck is going on&nbsp;
right now, Saitama and Tatsumaki just stand their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:10.120 --> 01:04:14.480
watching the most neuro divergent C-Class&nbsp;
scuffle they’ve ever seen. Questioning why&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:14.480 --> 01:04:19.880
Tatsumaki doesn't just let them all go at it,&nbsp;
she just yaps back that its none of his concern.

01:04:19.880 --> 01:04:24.640
Not listening, Saitama continues that back while&nbsp;
he was job hunting he wasn't even able to beat a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:24.640 --> 01:04:29.160
wolf level threat before starting proper&nbsp;
muscle training. Right now Fubuki’s team&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:29.160 --> 01:04:34.880
is all pathetically weak, however he thinks that&nbsp;
there is truly no telling what their limit may be.

01:04:34.880 --> 01:04:39.320
Agreeing with statement, Tatsumaki tears&nbsp;
her younger sister away and explains that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:39.320 --> 01:04:43.800
originally she came here to deal with Psykos.&nbsp;
In the end she overused to much power on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:43.800 --> 01:04:47.080
random battle and because of that has&nbsp;
decided to let everyone off the hook.

01:04:49.480 --> 01:04:53.920
Turning and glaring at the group, she exclaims&nbsp;
that if anything does happen to her sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:53.920 --> 01:04:57.720
then she will never forgive them! After&nbsp;
hearing them all agree, she finally turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:57.720 --> 01:05:02.280
to Saitama and tells him that this test of&nbsp;
theirs isn't exactly over yet. At any time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:02.280 --> 01:05:06.600
whenever she may feel like it, she might&nbsp;
show up and surprise him with another test!

01:05:06.600 --> 01:05:10.200
Suffering a level of depression&nbsp;
not yet reached by man, Saitama&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:10.200 --> 01:05:13.760
disagrees as thats the last damn thing he wants.

01:05:13.760 --> 01:05:15.720
Still nearby and having listened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:15.720 --> 01:05:20.480
Fubuki is left blown away that her&nbsp;
sister actually followed his orders!

01:05:20.480 --> 01:05:24.240
Moments later, Saitama tells&nbsp;
Tatsumaki to chill out and not&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:24.240 --> 01:05:28.280
destroy anything else before finally&nbsp;
making his way back to his apartment.

01:05:28.280 --> 01:05:31.600
Shooting up into the sky, we see that&nbsp;
after the intense battle has come to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:31.600 --> 01:05:35.600
an end and the landscape was destroyed,&nbsp;
apart from one minor whole in the base,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:35.600 --> 01:05:39.080
the entire association itself remained unscathed.

01:05:39.080 --> 01:05:43.000
Having made the long walk of shame home,&nbsp;
Saitama enters his apartment and comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:43.000 --> 01:05:46.640
to the conclusion he needs to get a&nbsp;
new pair of shoes and some clothes.

01:05:46.640 --> 01:05:51.880
Upon looking up though he, just like previously,&nbsp;
discovers that three A-class heroes; Forte,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:51.880 --> 01:05:56.360
Butterfly DX, and Chain’n’toad are waiting&nbsp;
for him! Wondering what the hell they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:56.360 --> 01:06:01.040
doing here now, Butterfly perks up and lets&nbsp;
him know that Forte has something to say!

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:06.120
Apologizing for their first meeting, Forte&nbsp;
legit starts glazing Saitama up, asking if&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:06.120 --> 01:06:10.560
he needs any new clothes or shoes and if he didnt&nbsp;
mind he could bring some old sets over for him!

01:06:10.560 --> 01:06:14.000
Creeped out with the sudden switch up,&nbsp;
Forte tries to say that its because they’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:14.000 --> 01:06:18.560
all A-Class buddies and he’s just trying to be&nbsp;
friendly! Sensing the awkwardness the group makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:18.560 --> 01:06:24.160
their leave, still Forte tells Saitama that if&nbsp;
anything does bother him, come and let him know!

01:06:24.160 --> 01:06:28.720
After the trio of heroes departed from Saitama’s&nbsp;
apartment, Butterfly DX expressed his bewilderment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:28.720 --> 01:06:33.680
over Forte’s abrupt change, questioning if the&nbsp;
car knocked a different personality into him.

01:06:33.680 --> 01:06:37.400
Knowing a greater secret though, Forte&nbsp;
disclosed that he witnessed Saitama’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:37.400 --> 01:06:41.800
fighting while at the hospital. Compared to&nbsp;
them, his movements were out of this world&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:41.800 --> 01:06:46.400
and he honestly doubts all 3 of them would even&nbsp;
last 10 seconds against him in a true fight.

01:06:46.400 --> 01:06:51.560
Telling him to relax, Forte continues elaborating&nbsp;
on how those previous earthquakes weren’t caused&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:51.560 --> 01:06:56.640
by mere monsters. It was the impact from his&nbsp;
fighting! Turning and pointing out the pets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:56.640 --> 01:07:02.400
he states that they better look after them and&nbsp;
do their best to get Saitama on their side!

01:07:02.400 --> 01:07:07.200
At the Demon-Level Monster Containment Level,&nbsp;
three A-class heroes – Stinger, Lightning Max,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:07.200 --> 01:07:11.160
and Blue Fire arrived to investigate the&nbsp;
situation. After inspecting the mess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:11.160 --> 01:07:16.200
Lighting Max assumes that most of the monsters&nbsp;
on this floor were wiped out by each other. Blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:16.200 --> 01:07:20.520
who was also investigating couldn't come to&nbsp;
a solid conclusion on why association would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:20.520 --> 01:07:25.840
take such risks containing a bunch of dangerous&nbsp;
monsters below them. The Fubuki group though try&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:25.840 --> 01:07:31.000
explaining that it wasn't a monster fight and&nbsp;
instead it was a single A-Class who took them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:37.760
all out. Asking if they all just saw something,&nbsp;
they re-iterate that they were telling the truth!

01:07:37.760 --> 01:07:42.600
In the meantime, the other Fubuki members confront&nbsp;
the executives of the Hero Association and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:42.600 --> 01:07:47.360
accuse them of defiantly knowing something about&nbsp;
Tsukuyomi. Instead of fessing up, the executives&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:47.360 --> 01:07:51.600
explain that they just happened to have some&nbsp;
spare time and wanted to check the area out.

01:07:51.600 --> 01:07:55.560
Realizing that they probably fell for a cruel&nbsp;
scheme, Gearsper explains to the other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:55.560 --> 01:08:01.000
around that Tsukuyomi is the name of a secret&nbsp;
society. The only reason he even knows of it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:06.200
because there has been an urban legend about them&nbsp;
inside of the psychic circles. However he thinks&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:06.200 --> 01:08:10.440
that its all just a complete farce. Instead it&nbsp;
makes more sense for the surviving members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:10.440 --> 01:08:15.800
the monster association to come back and kidnap&nbsp;
their leader under the guise of some new group.

01:08:15.800 --> 01:08:20.840
With everyone somewhat agreeing with his&nbsp;
statement, Fubuki calls out to Mr McCoy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:20.840 --> 01:08:25.120
one of the executives to have a chat&nbsp;
about something. Entering another room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:25.120 --> 01:08:29.400
Fubuki confronts McCoy and asks him what&nbsp;
the hell he’s planning here. If it wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:29.400 --> 01:08:33.520
for ‘her’, all of the members of her group&nbsp;
would've been turned into monster food.

01:08:33.520 --> 01:08:38.680
Fessing up, McCoy goes on to detail that they’ve&nbsp;
been keeping monsters here for a top-secret weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:38.680 --> 01:08:44.040
that is currently being designed by Metal Bat.&nbsp;
Wanting more info, Fubuki raises a document and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:44.040 --> 01:08:48.360
asks for what in the world this massive&nbsp;
sum of money paid to the association was.

01:08:48.360 --> 01:08:52.800
Sweating balls over being found out,&nbsp;
Fubuki’s genius hacker notes that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:52.800 --> 01:08:56.680
lines of code he has are probably some of&nbsp;
the worst he’s ever seen. To which Fubuki&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:56.680 --> 01:09:00.600
jokes that it would be such a scandal for&nbsp;
the world to find out about this news.

01:09:00.600 --> 01:09:05.480
Immediately, Mr McCoy drops his act and asks&nbsp;
what it is that Fubuki actually wants. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:05.480 --> 01:09:09.600
a grin of pleasure, Fubuki goes on to&nbsp;
lay out her devious plan. Pretty much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:09.600 --> 01:09:13.840
she wants to take all of the monsters that have&nbsp;
died, turn the cams off and lay them out up on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:13.840 --> 01:09:18.480
the surface. That way, Tatsumaki’s rampage&nbsp;
can be marked off as her fighting against&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:18.480 --> 01:09:22.800
these demon level threats. Plus if they&nbsp;
manage to fix both of those issues at once,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:22.800 --> 01:09:26.400
all of the rich folk will gain some trust&nbsp;
back in the security of their homes.

01:09:28.320 --> 01:09:33.400
Starting to cackle, McCoy agree’s&nbsp;
with Fubuki’s proposal, and Tatsumaki&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:33.400 --> 01:09:38.120
subsequently brought the monster remains to&nbsp;
the surface, as per the agreement. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:38.120 --> 01:09:43.080
it turned out to be a ruse, as one of the&nbsp;
remains had a special someone hidden inside.

01:09:43.800 --> 01:09:45.920
Pulling up next to a clump of monster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:45.920 --> 01:09:50.640
Fubuki used her abilities to tear hear old&nbsp;
friend out and into her car. Following this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:50.640 --> 01:09:54.960
the group steps on the gas and accomplishes&nbsp;
their original goal they set out to achieve.

01:10:00.800 --> 01:10:05.120
Simultaneously, the news broadcast of the&nbsp;
incident brought Tatsumaki into the spotlight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:05.120 --> 01:10:11.000
as apparently she repelled them all on her own.&nbsp;
All around the city, literally everyone except&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:17.240
one man was overjoyed for this massive feat. Of&nbsp;
course, Saitama and subsequently Genos think its&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:17.240 --> 01:10:22.840
complete crap. Genos even gets on the phone to&nbsp;
file a major complaint for this incredulous act.

01:10:22.840 --> 01:10:26.200
In the aftermath of the incident, the Hero&nbsp;
Association headquarters soon discovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:26.200 --> 01:10:30.680
that Psykos had gone missing. Apparently&nbsp;
she was able to escape through a hole in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:30.680 --> 01:10:34.720
the floor or ceiling of the parking lot.&nbsp;
Being called there to answer for this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:34.720 --> 01:10:42.560
Tatsumaki feigned responsibility and&nbsp;
began searching for the missing esper.

01:10:42.560 --> 01:10:51.320
Watching her leave and with a grin on his&nbsp;
face, McCoy calls out to her saying that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:51.320 --> 01:10:56.440
didnt realize she could be o so remorseful.&nbsp;
Its almost as if she’s being strangely kind!

01:10:57.280 --> 01:10:59.120
Turning and looking more cooked than ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:59.120 --> 01:11:03.680
Tatsumaki leaves saying that its just&nbsp;
somedays she happens to be in a good mood!

01:11:03.680 --> 01:11:06.520
Meanwhile, Child Emperor who thought&nbsp;
the incident was kinda sussy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:07.280 --> 01:11:09.480
did a little digging. After a little hacking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:11.400 --> 01:11:16.400
he quickly came to see that the entire&nbsp;
incident was nothing but fraud and coverups!

